BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c4182696-d11c-4d57-8433-294573f29c7d
DTSTAMP:20260224T200348Z
DTSTART:20260305T003000Z
DTEND:20260305T013000Z
SUMMARY:Free Food @ ACM - Meeting #7, Movie Night: The Internet's Own Boy (2014)
DESCRIPTION:Join the ACM for a movie night, where we'll be watching "The Internet's Own Boy (2014)", a documentary about programming prodigy and information activist Aaron Swartz. *Note: An RSVP is required, for pizza ordering purposes.  Movie Description: "He helped develop the Internet Protocol RSS and was a co-founder of Reddit. Chronicling his pioneering efforts crusading for open access and free speech and the resulting legal nightmare and tragedy that ensued, The Internet's Own Boy is a dynamic and moving portrait of a brilliant tech millionaire who renounced the values of Silicon Valley startup culture and used technology to tirelessly fight for social justice, no matter what the cost."  Perks:  - Fun Technology Movie  - Pizza  - ACM
LOCATION:Julian Hall, Room 31
END:VEVENT
